Retained from the upstream project
----------------------------------
  * MediaPipe Hands integration and the real-time capture loop
  * Landmark pre-processing (wrist-relative coordinates, flattening, normalisation)
  * Landmark and bounding-box drawing code
  * utils/cvfpscalc.py (FPS counter)
  * The KeyPointClassifier TFLite wrapper
  * The overall structure of the training notebook and its TFLite quantisation step

Modifications made in this work
-------------------------------
  * Retargeted the classifier from the upstream sample gesture set to Indian Sign
    Language fingerspelling: 36 classes covering the digits 0-9 and the letters A-Z.
  * Collected a new training dataset of 117,139 labelled landmark vectors by live
    webcam capture (model/keypoint_classifier/keypoint.csv.gz), replacing the
    upstream sample data, and retrained the classifier on it. The trained weights
    (keypoint_classifier.hdf5) and quantised model (keypoint_classifier.tflite)
    in this repository are the results of that training.
  * Rewrote model/keypoint_classifier/keypoint_classifier_label.csv for the 36 ISL
    classes.
  * Extended select_mode() in app.py so that the a-z keys map to class ids 10-35,
    allowing the letter classes to be recorded in logging mode; widened the class-id
    range accepted by logging_csv() accordingly.
  * Removed the point-history (dynamic finger gesture) classifier and its associated
    model, dataset, notebook and drawing code, which are not used for static
    fingerspelling recognition.
  * Added project documentation: report, conference abstract, block diagram,
    flowcharts, design document, implementation notes and literature survey
    (docs/).
  * Added scripts/prepare_dataset.py, requirements.txt and this notice.

